-- title:
--   Valuation subring of a height-one prime of a normal Noetherian domain
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a Noetherian integrally closed domain and $K$ a field equipped with a $C$-algebra structure making it the fraction field of $C$, and let $P \subseteq C$ be a prime ideal of height $1$. The assertion is the existence of a valuation subring $V \subseteq K$ with the following five properties. First, an element $x \in K$ lies in $V$ precisely when there are $c, s \in C$ with $s \notin P$ and $x \cdot s = c$ in $K$, so that $V$ is the image of the localisation of $C$ at $P$ inside $K$. Second, the image of $C$ in $K$ is contained in $V$. Third, for $c \in C$ the image of $c$ is a nonunit of $V$ exactly when $c \in P$; thus the centre of $V$ on $C$ is $P$. Fourth, for every $\varpi \in P$, the condition that every nonunit $f$ of $V$ can be written $f = \varpi g$ with $g \in V$ holds if and only if the maximal ideal of $\mathrm{Localization.AtPrime}\ P$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$. Fifth, there is a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the residue field of the local ring $V$ to the residue field $\kappa(P)$ of $P$ such that for every $c \in C$ whose image lies in $V$, $\iota$ carries the residue class of that image to the image of $c$ in $\kappa(P)$.
--
--   This packages the classical fact that the localisation $C_P$ of a normal Noetherian domain at a height-one prime is a discrete valuation ring, presented as a valuation subring of the fraction field together with the dictionary between that subring and the prime $P$: membership, centre, uniformisers and residue field. It serves as the translation between statements typed on height-one primes of normal rings and statements typed on valuation subrings of a function field, and is used in the analysis of integral models, for instance by [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.map_span_eq_maximalIdeal_localization_atPrime_of_forall_valuationSubring_mul_inv_mem`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.map_span_eq_maximalIdeal_localization_atPrime_of_forall_valuationSubring_mul_inv_mem).
